[2026-08-30T14:59:04.917Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c0769e1ed77afabd13df76ecc50c602d] Topic: Set up shadcn/ui component library with dark-only Ghost AI theme tokens
[2026-08-30T14:59:04.917Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c0769e1ed77afabd13df76ecc50c602d]   Trigger:   The project needed its foundational design system in place before any feature UI could be built — a component library and a color theme matching the intended dark, ghost-themed visual identity for the app.
[2026-08-30T14:59:04.917Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c0769e1ed77afabd13df76ecc50c602d]   Response:  - Initialized shadcn/ui via `components.json` (style `base-nova`, neutral base color, RSC + CSS variables enabled) and installed `lucide-react`; added seven generated primitives to `components/ui/` — Button, Card, Dialog, Input, Tabs, Textarea, and ScrollArea — left unmodified per convention.
- Created `lib/utils.ts` exporting a `cn()` helper built on `clsx` and `tailwind-merge` for safely combining Tailwind class strings.
- Rewrote `app/globals.css` so the full Ghost AI dark palette (backgrounds, text, accent, AI, and state colors) lives once in `:root` with no light or `.dark` variant, wiring the same values into both shadcn's semantic design tokens (background, card, primary, border, etc.) and the app's own custom utility names (`bg-base`, `text-copy-primary`, `border-surface-border`, `text-brand`, and similar).
[2026-08-30T14:59:04.917Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c0769e1ed77afabd13df76ecc50c602d]   Decisions: - **Single dark-only theme source**: rather than supporting a toggleable light/dark mode, the palette was defined once and mapped onto every consumer (shadcn tokens and custom utility classes), keeping styling consistent and eliminating a class of bugs where components accidentally pick up default light theming.
- **No hand-editing of generated components**: the shadcn-generated files in `components/ui/` are treated as vendor code; any custom behavior needed later must be built by wrapping or extending them elsewhere, keeping future upgrades from the component library conflict-free.
